# .NET Framework → .NET 8 Migration: `EventProcessor`

## Critical Issues in the Original Code

| Issue | .NET 8 Impact |
|-------|---------------|
| `Thread.Abort()` | Throws `PlatformNotSupportedException` — **removed entirely** |
| `Thread.Interrupt()` | Still works but unreliable; only throws during managed blocking calls |
| `ManualResetEvent` + `lock` + `Queue` | Reinvents what `BlockingCollection<T>` already does |
| Race condition | Multiple `Enqueue` calls between `WaitOne`/`Reset` lose items |

## Migrated Code (.NET 8)

```csharp
using System.Threading.Channels;

public class EventProcessor : IAsyncDisposable
{
    private readonly Channel<string> _channel = Channel.CreateUnbounded<string>();
    private Task? _runTask;
    private CancellationTokenSource? _cts;

    public void Start()
    {
        _cts = new CancellationTokenSource();
        _runTask = Task.Run(() => RunLoopAsync(_cts.Token));
    }

    private async Task RunLoopAsync(CancellationToken ct)
    {
        await foreach (var item in _channel.Reader.ReadAllAsync(ct))
        {
            Handle(item);
        }
    }

    public void Enqueue(string item)
    {
        if (!_channel.Writer.TryWrite(item))
            throw new InvalidOperationException("Channel is closed.");
    }

    public async ValueTask DisposeAsync()
    {
        _channel.Writer.Complete();          // signal no more items
        _cts?.Cancel();                      // cancel if blocked waiting
        if (_runTask is not null)
            await _runTask.ConfigureAwait(false);
        _cts?.Dispose();
    }

    public async Task StopAsync(TimeSpan? timeout = null)
    {
        _channel.Writer.Complete();
        _cts?.Cancel();
        if (_runTask is not null)
        {
            var delay = Task.Delay(timeout ?? TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
            if (await Task.WhenAny(_runTask, delay) == delay)
                throw new TimeoutException("EventProcessor did not stop in time.");
        }
        _cts?.Dispose();
    }

    private void Handle(string item) { /* your logic */ }
}
```

## Key Migration Decisions

**1. `Thread.Abort` → `CancellationToken`**
Cooperative cancellation replaces forced thread termination. `ReadAllAsync(ct)` throws `OperationCanceledException` when cancelled — no risk of corrupted state.

**2. `ManualResetEvent` + `Queue` + `lock` → `Channel<T>`**
`Channel<T>` is a thread-safe, high-performance async producer/consumer queue. It eliminates the race condition where multiple `Set()` calls between `WaitOne`/`Reset` caused lost items.

**3. `Thread` → `Task.Run`**
Uses the thread pool instead of a dedicated thread, integrating with `async/await`.

**4. `Stop()` → `StopAsync()` + `IAsyncDisposable`**
Graceful shutdown: complete the channel (drain remaining items), then cancel if still blocked.

## If You Need a Synchronous API

```csharp
// Drop-in replacement using BlockingCollection (synchronous equivalent)
public class EventProcessorSync : IDisposable
{
    private readonly BlockingCollection<string> _queue = new();
    private readonly CancellationTokenSource _cts = new();
    private Thread? _thread;

    public void Start()
    {
        _thread = new Thread(RunLoop) { IsBackground = true };
        _thread.Start();
    }

    private void RunLoop()
    {
        try
        {
            foreach (var item in _queue.GetConsumingEnumerable(_cts.Token))
                Handle(item);
        }
        catch (OperationCanceledException) { }
    }

    public void Enqueue(string item) => _queue.Add(item);

    public void Stop()
    {
        _queue.CompleteAdding();
        _cts.Cancel();
        if (!_thread?.Join(5000) ?? false)
            throw new TimeoutException("Worker did not stop in time.");
    }

    public void Dispose() { Stop(); _cts.Dispose(); _queue.Dispose(); }
    private void Handle(string item) { /* your logic */ }
}
```

## Pitfall Summary

| Pitfall | Recommendation |
|---------|---------------|
| Replacing `Abort` with `Environment.Exit` | Don't — use `CancellationToken` |
| Catching `ThreadAbortException` | No longer thrown; remove those catch blocks |
| `Thread.Interrupt` in WaitOne | Unreliable in .NET 8; use cancellation tokens |
| Lost items from `Set`/`Reset` race | `Channel` and `BlockingCollection` are immune |
| Blocking in async context | Use `Channel<T>` (async) or `BlockingCollection` (sync), not both |
